        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Linear trend analysis over time-windowed aggregates.</para>
<para>The method first partitions [from, to) into tumbling windows of window_size_ms (auto-derived as range/10 when window_size_ms is 0), computes the requested aggregate per window, and then performs an ordinary-least-squares regression of value vs. window centre time.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>table</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Source table. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>measure_field</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>JSON field to aggregate (uses SUM by default). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>from</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Range start (inclusive, ms epoch). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>to</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Range end (exclusive, ms epoch). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>window_size_ms</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Tumbling window size for bucketing; 0 = auto. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1temporal_1_1_trend_result" kindref="compound">TrendResult</ref> with slope, intercept, and r². </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
